.TH LUS-AGENTS 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-agents \- set a project up for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus agents\fR init [dir]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds instructions for writing and testing Lus to a project, where coding agents read them.
The command writes the agent skills of the running version into \fBdir/.agents/skills\fR and links \fB.claude/skills\fR to them, then adds a Lus section to \fBAGENTS.md\fR.
\fBdir\fR defaults to the current directory.
Running the command again updates the skills.
The agents page lists the skills and the prompts to start from.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The skills were written.
.TP
1
A file cannot be written.
.TP
2
The arguments are malformed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-agents, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
